{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_singleton_manager_clustersingletonmanager", "label": "ClusterSingletonManager", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/cluster/singleton/manager.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The per-node actor that owns the singleton election logic; every node runs one, only the host's manager has an active singleton child."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_singleton_manager_host_election", "label": "The host is the first address-ordered up-member", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/cluster/singleton/manager.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Without a role the host is the leader; with one it is the first up-member carrying that role \u2014 not \"the leader if it happens to carry the role\", which would leave the singleton hosted nowhere whenever the elected leader lacked it. Both forms read the same address-ordered list, so every node independently picks the same node."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_singleton_manager_singletonmanagerpath", "label": "singletonManagerPath naming convention", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/cluster/singleton/manager.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The proxy uses the well-known path to find the manager on the hosting node; misnaming is silent breakage."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_singleton_manager_trigger_events", "label": "Host-changing trigger event set", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/cluster/singleton/manager.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "LeaderChanged, SelfUp, MemberUp and MemberDown/Left/Removed. MemberJoined and MemberWeaklyUp are excluded because neither joining nor weakly-up members appear in upMembers(). Before v0.17.0 the trigger was LeaderChanged alone, and a role-carrying member joining below a role-less leader settled the cluster on two live singletons."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_singleton_manager_unreachability_not_trigger", "label": "Unreachability is deliberately not a trigger", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/cluster/singleton/manager.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Every event in the set states a membership fact the whole cluster converges on. Unreachability is one node's failure detector, and the member it is about cannot hear the peers that formed the opinion \u2014 a manager reconciling on it would promote itself while the incumbent kept its child, and no leader moves to resolve it. Availability is recoverable and bounded by downing; a second live singleton is neither."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_singleton_manager_no_lease_path", "label": "No-lease hand-over path", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/cluster/singleton/manager.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The manager asks every eligible peer to stand down rather than the previous host, because a node that has just joined has no notion of a previous host and joining is the common case; the outgoing host is by definition the first member of that set, so asking all of them cannot miss it."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_singleton_manager_handoverrequest", "label": "singleton.HandOverRequest", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/cluster/singleton/manager.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Re-sent every half second while outstanding, because a cluster envelope is fire-and-forget and a single frame can be dropped behind a handshake."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_singleton_manager_handoveracknowledgment", "label": "singleton.HandOverAcknowledgment", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/cluster/singleton/manager.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A node answers only once it holds no instance and none of its own is still stopping, so the answer is about a completed postStop, not about a PoisonPill having been enqueued."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_singleton_manager_handovertimeoutms", "label": "handOverTimeoutMs", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/cluster/singleton/manager.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Bounds the wait and the wait ends in a spawn either way. Hosting anyway means the uniqueness invariant was not proven \u2014 a different statement from upheld, and the warning should be read as exactly that."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_singleton_manager_lease_path", "label": "Lease-gated spawn path", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/cluster/singleton/manager.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Adds an async gate: internal events rather than inline awaits drive the transitions, so concurrent cluster events cannot interleave with an in-flight acquire."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_singleton_manager_lease_lost", "label": "Lease lost handling", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/cluster/singleton/manager.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The manager stops the singleton with a PoisonPill and only re-attempts acquire once that has finished. Before v0.17.0 it re-acquired immediately and the consequence was not two instances but zero: the spawn was refused because a stop was in flight, the reconcile read \"lease held\" as \"already running\", and the manager renewed a lease over no singleton permanently."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_singleton_manager_stepping_down", "label": "Stepping down with a lease", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/cluster/singleton/manager.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The release is what gives a follower permission to spawn, so it happens only once this node's instance has genuinely terminated; releasing on PoisonPill enqueue gave the whole guarantee away one line early."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_singleton_manager_restartontermination", "label": "restartOnTermination latch", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/cluster/singleton/manager.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The opt-out has to be a latch rather than the absence of a trigger: the manager decides to spawn from \"I am the host and have no child\", which cannot tell a terminal stop apart from never having started."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_singleton_manager_message_hold", "label": "Holding messages while elected but instance-less", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/cluster/singleton/manager.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Capped at 1000 messages and two seconds. The hold cannot be conditional on the manager agreeing that it hosts, because the window exists precisely because it does not agree yet and an incomplete view is not evidence; a manager that opted out of hosting is the one case that is evidence, and it dead-letters immediately."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_singleton_manager_deadletters", "label": "Dead letters for un-hostable messages", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/cluster/singleton/manager.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Not dropped silently, so it shows up wherever dead letters are already watched. Before v0.17.0 the manager logged a warning per message and dropped it, making the loss invisible to everything but the log."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_singleton_manager_handover_authorization", "label": "Who may ask for a hand-over", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/cluster/singleton/manager.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Honoured only from a transport-verified address, and a node that believes it hosts stands down only for a peer that sorts before it \u2014 the host is the first address-ordered member of the eligible set, so a legitimate incoming host always sorts first. Neither substitutes for authenticating the cluster wire, which carries no credential today."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_singleton_manager_acquireretryintervalms", "label": "acquireRetryIntervalMs", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/cluster/singleton/manager.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "0 does not disable retries \u2014 there is no disable switch; a non-positive value is rejected with an OptionsError up front."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_singleton_manager_child_death_watch", "label": "Death-watching the singleton child", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/cluster/singleton/manager.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A one-second backoff before re-spawn, because a supervision-budget death would otherwise restart that budget too and turn a crash-looping singleton into a hot loop. The alternative is a silent, permanent, cluster-wide outage of the one component whose purpose is availability-of-one."}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_singleton_manager_clustersingletonmanager", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_singleton_manager_host_election", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/cluster/singleton/manager.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_singleton_manager_clustersingletonmanager", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_singleton_manager_singletonmanagerpath", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/cluster/singleton/manager.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_singleton_manager_clustersingletonmanager", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_singleton_manager_trigger_events", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/cluster/singleton/manager.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_singleton_manager_trigger_events", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_singleton_manager_unreachability_not_trigger", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/cluster/singleton/manager.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_singleton_manager_host_election", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_singleton_manager_trigger_events", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/cluster/singleton/manager.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_singleton_manager_clustersingletonmanager", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_singleton_manager_no_lease_path", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/cluster/singleton/manager.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_singleton_manager_no_lease_path", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_singleton_manager_handoverrequest", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/cluster/singleton/manager.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_singleton_manager_handoverrequest", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_singleton_manager_handoveracknowledgment", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/cluster/singleton/manager.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_singleton_manager_no_lease_path", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_singleton_manager_handovertimeoutms", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/cluster/singleton/manager.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_singleton_manager_clustersingletonmanager", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_singleton_manager_lease_path", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/cluster/singleton/manager.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_singleton_manager_lease_path", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_singleton_manager_lease_lost", "relation": "refe